## The task
Issue NIFI-12082 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: Schema in JsonTreeReader documentation is invalid

The schema in the JsonTreeReader documentation
{code:java}
{
    "namespace": "nifi",
    "name": "person",
    "type": "record",
    "fields": [
        { "name": "id", "type": "int" },
        { "name": "name", "type": "string" },
        { "name": "gender", "type": "string" },
        { "name": "dob", "type": {
            "type": "int",
            "logicalType": "date"
        }},
        { "name": "siblings", "type": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
                "type": "record",
                "fields": [
                    { "name": "name", "type": "string" }
                ]
            }
        }}
    ]
}  {code}
when loaded in a AvroSchemaRegistry results with the error message not a valid schema.

The documentation should be corrected to have a schema that will load.

Screenshot attached

## Their verdict
- APPROVED

## The task
Issue NIFI-13838 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Allow Change Version on a ghosted component when bundle becomes available

Current the logic for allowing Change Version on a component is triggered when multiple bundles are available. Originally this made sense, but now that NARs can be auto-loaded while NiFi is running, a component that is ghosted may now be able to be unghosted, but we are showing the Change Version menu because only 1 bundle is available.

