- That should not be the case. We did change things so that parameter values coming via a provider are no longer persisted on disk (only kept in memory for better security). In case of a reboot, when NiFi is starting all of the components, the fetch will be executed automatically on the provider(s) to have the values of the parameters. But if a parameter has been deleted on the provider side (say AWS Secret Manager), you'd have to manually call the fetch to have it removed from the parameter context, otherwise it'd remain there with an empty value. If you observe something else, let me know.

