Issue NIFI-15667 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Support plain text secrets in AWS Secrets Manager Parameter Provider

When a secret stored in AWS Secrets Manager is not a JSON key/value object (e.g., a PEM-encoded private key stored via --secret-string file://path/to/key.pem), the parameter provider silently discards it. This should be supported and the parameter name and group name should both be set to the secret name.

