## The task
Issue NIFI-15685 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: ListS3 V1 pagination fails when delimiter is not set causing infinite loop for buckets with more than 1000 objects
Area: Extensions

In S3ObjectBucketLister.setNextMarker() (the V1 lister), the code unconditionally used listObjectsResponse.nextMarker() as the pagination marker. Per the AWS S3 ListObjects V1 API, nextMarker is only populated when a delimiter is specified in the request. Without a delimiter, nextMarker() returns null, which resets the listing back to the beginning of the bucket, creating an infinite loop re-fetching the same first page of objects.

