## The task
Issue NIFI-15830 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Fix local change detection for versioned process groups when setting previously unset properties
Area: Flow Versioning

The *isPropertyAddedFromMigration* method in *FlowDifferenceFilters* (introduced by NIFI-15776) is too broad. It classifies every *PROPERTY_ADDED* diff for a non-dynamic property as an environmental change, without checking whether the property already existed in the versioned snapshot. When a user sets a previously-unset property (null to value), the comparator produces {*}PROPERTY_ADDED{*}, and the filter incorrectly swallows it.

