## The task
Issue NIFI-16333 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Invalidate Secrets Manager cache when starting a Connector

At the moment if a connector is stopped and restarted, it does not ensure that its referenced secrets would be refreshed as we may be using the cached value from when the connector was running. The goal of this change is to bypass the secrets manager caching when the connector starts to make sure we have refreshed values. This can be used as a way to address secrets rotation by simply restarting the connector.

