Title: EL toDate() always uses local timezone
Area: Core Framework

I use a parameter date "20250601". Nifi is running in CEST timezone.
Now I need to generate a date in UTC based on the parameter "date".

If I use UpdateAttribute Processor with 
${date:toDate(''yyyyMMdd,'UTC')}, it generates the timestamp "Sun Jun 01 00:00:00 CEST 2025". I would expect "Sun Jun 01 *02:00:00* CEST 2025".

I also already tested it with timezone "Europe/Kiev" or "America/Detroit", I always get "Sun Jun 01 00:00:00 CEST 2025".

It looks, that this Nifi expression Language method "toDate" always uses the local timezone.

In release 1.23.2 it was working fine.

