## The task
Issue NIFI-15214 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Refactor site-to-site-client HTTP using Java HttpClient
Area: Core Framework

The {{nifi-site-to-site-client}} depends on both the synchronous and asynchronous Apache HttpClient 4 libraries to implement communication for Site-to-Site transfer over HTTP. The standard Java HttpClient class supports both synchronous and asynchronous request handling, providing the opportunity to streamline the implementation and remove dependencies on the Apache HttpClient libraries. Refactoring to use the Java HttpClient should also remove the need to include Apache HttpClient 4 dependencies in the {{nifi-framework-nar}}.

