    ts timestamptz NOT NULL
); {code}
 

Input:
{code:java}
{
    "ts": 1765056655230
} {code}
Timestamp loaded into PostgreSQL: `{color:#00875a}2025-12-06 16:30:55.230 -0500{color}`

 

Input:
{code:java}
{
    "ts": 1765056655230.746 
}  {code}
Timestamp loaded into PostgreSQL: `{color:#FF0000}57902-06-03 07:20:30746. -0400{color}`

 

The information tip for the Timestamp Format field in the JsonTreeReader Controller Service indicates that timestamp fields are assumed to be the epoch in milliseconds unless a time format is specified:

!image-2025-12-06-19-30-42-959.png|width=584,height=235!

 

The behavior was introduced in: NIFI-12710

