## The task
Issue NIFI-15341 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: External Controller Service resolution can break with property migration
Area: Core Framework

When importing or replacing a Process Group, External Controller Services can fail to resolve if a component property was renamed between the versioned flow and the currently installed bundle using property migration.

To reproduce in 2.4.0 or later, download attached JSON file representing a Process Group Replace request.  Then log into NiFi and copy the Bearer token.  Then create a new blank process group in NiFi and copy its identifier for below.

Next, create a new StandardRestrictedSSLContextService at the root canvas and name it "SSL Context Service".

{code:java}
BEARER_TOKEN=<paste bearer token>
PG_ID=<pg id>

curl -k -vv -X POST https://localhost:8443/nifi-api/process-groups/$PG_ID/replace-requests -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Authorization: Bearer $BEARER_TOKEN" -d [user]
{code}

Observe that the SSL Context Service property in the MongoDBControllerService now references a UUID instead of the "SSL Context Service" service.

