Issue NIFI-16225 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: Regression of "Proxified SFTP processors resolve hostnames and pass IP instead of FQDN in HTTP headers" (NIFI-14068)

In https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/NIFI-14068, domain name handling for SFTP proxy access was fixed by sending a DNS address instead of a resolved IP address to SOCKS proxies.

However, this fix seems to have regressed with the switch to Apache MINA SSHD in https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/NIFI-14720, as the same code path is no longer used.

