## The task
Issue NIFI-16380 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Add Records Metrics to ConsumeKinesis
Area: Extensions

Following the pattern of {{{}ConsumeKafka{}}}, the {{ConsumeKinesis}} Processor should track lag and record metrics for each invocation. The Map of attributes for Counters and Gauges should include the Kinesis Stream and Shard information.

The metrics should include the following:
 * kinesis.bytes.consumed
 ** Type: Counter
 * kinesis.records.consumed
 ** Type: Counter
 * kinesis.consumer.milliseconds.behind
 ** Type: Gauge
 * kinesis.records.parsed.errors
 ** Type: Counter

Kinesis supports the concept of [MillisBehindLatest|https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/API_GetRecords.html#API_GetRecords_ResponseSyntax] to indicate the number milliseconds behind the consumer is from the latest record in the stream. This is a loose indicator of lag because it does not provide the number of records and interpreting the number requires an understanding of expected periodicity for records added to the Kinesis Stream.

