## The task
Issue NIFI-16384 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: Replace use of deprecated BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory constructor with API suggested replacement

The NIFI-16340 upgrade of Bouncycastle from 1.85 to 1.86 resulted in the following warning messages.

{code:java}
[WARNING] /home/runner/work/nifi/nifi/nifi-extension-bundles/nifi-pgp-bundle/nifi-pgp-processors/src/main/java/org/apache/nifi/processors/pgp/DecryptContentPGP.java:[420,75] [deprecation] BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory(PGPPrivateKey) in BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory has been deprecated
[WARNING] /home/runner/work/nifi/nifi/nifi-extension-bundles/nifi-pgp-bundle/nifi-pgp-processors/src/test/java/org/apache/nifi/processors/pgp/EncryptContentPGPTest.java:[330,63] [deprecation] BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory(PGPPrivateKey) in BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory has been deprecated
{code}

Bouncycastle  1.86 deprecated the use of the  BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory which takes a PGPPrivateKey in favor of a constructor which takes a PGPKeyPair as seen in the [javadocs|https://javadoc.io/doc/org.bouncycastle/bcpg-jdk18on/latest/org/bouncycastle/openpgp/operator/bc/BcPublicKeyDataDecryptorFactory.html]. 
The purpose of this ticket is to switch over to the use of the new constructor.

