## The task
Issue NIFI-11576 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: XMLReader not handling namespaced attributes correctly (xmlns:foo="")

Supposing we have
{code:java}
<wd:report_data xmlns:wd="">
    <wd:record>
        <wd:foo wd:bar="bar content">foo content</wd:foo>
    </wd:record>
</wd:report_data> {code}
`XMLReader` recognizes `foo content` and extracts it correctly but is failing to pick up `bar content`.

Workaround is to remove the NS for attr's:  `<wd:foo bar="bar content">foo content</wd:foo>`

More details on how to repro in comments.

## What this person changed
- NIFI-11576 Fixed XMLReader to now allow for handling name spaced attributes when the schema is inferred.
