## The task
Issue NIFI-15553 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: Replace the use of jars in TestExecuteStreamCommand with the use of java files

Historically the only way to run a Java file in TestExecuteStreamCommand was to create a jar file with the Java file. Since Java 11 its possible to run a single-file Java program without the need for javac. Hence the tests in TestExecuteStreamCommand no longer need jars but can run the single Java files with the java command.

The point of this ticket is to remove the use of jars in TestExecuteStreamCommand and replace their use with the single Java files.

