## The task
Issue NIFI-15816 (Task, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Connector wizard
Area: Core UI

To edit a connector's configuration, a wizard-like experience should be exposed to the user. The connector metadata should drive the wizard UI. Consideration should be made to support custom connector UIs.

## Their verdict
- CHANGES_REQUESTED: Thanks for the PR [user]!

I've noted a couple items below. Also, Would it be possible to avoid use of `any` where we already have a type defined. I think we probably already have many defined, just a matter of using them (specific ones dealing with the property descriptors).

Also, I noted the formatting of the markdown step documentation isn't quite right and the are some font size and layout issues in the property group card in the summary page of the wizard.
- APPROVED: Thanks for the updates [user]!

## What they pointed at in the code
- nifi-frontend/src/main/frontend/libs/shared/src/components/connector-wizard/connector-wizard.component.ts:154 — `getCustomStepTemplate` builds the map only when empty. If `contentChildren`/`WizardCustomStepDirective` changes after first use, the map becomes stale.

```
private customStepMap = computed(() => {
    const map = new Map<string, TemplateRef<{ $implicit: string }>>();
    for (const dir of this.customStepDirectives()) {
        map.set(dir.stepName(), dir.templateRef);
    }
    return map;
});
getCustomStepTemplate(stepName: string): TemplateRef<{ $implicit: string }> | null {
    return this.customStepMap().get(stepName) ?? null;
}
```
- nifi-frontend/src/main/frontend/libs/shared/src/components/wizard/wizard.component.ts:51 — Could we use signal output here?

