## The task
Issue NIFI-14654 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: When Stateless group is stopped, processors may be stopped before session commit callbacks are called
Area: Core Framework

If a Processor commits a session using {{ProcessSession.commitAsync(Runnable, Consumer<Throwable>)}} but the Stateless Process Group is stopped, sometimes the Processor's [user] method is called before the Runnable or Consumer<Throwable> is called. This can cause the [user] method to behave incorrectly, effectively running while the Processor is still being triggered.

