## The task
Issue NIFI-14673 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: When using Stateless Execution Engine, each start/stop causes duplication of bulletins
Area: Core Framework

When using a Process Group configured with a Stateless Execution Engine, each time that you stop/start the Process Group, we appear to increase the number of bulletins per log message by 1.

For example, create a flow with a GenerateFlowFile -> LogMessage and configure for Stateless Execution Engine. Set Bulletin Level on LogMessage to INFO.

Run the stateless flow, and the message will be logged once.

Stop it and run again. Now, for each FlowFile, there will be 2 bulletins.

Stop and run again. Now, for each FlowFile, there will be 3 bulletins, and so on.

