Issue NIFI-16341 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Make controller service disable scheduler test deterministic
Area: Core Framework

{{TestStandardProcessScheduler.validateNeverEnablingServiceCanStillBeDisabled()}} intermittently fails with {{expected: <0> but was: <1>}} on the {{disableInvocationCount()}} assertion.

After [NIFI-16288], disabling a Controller Service that is still in {{ENABLING}} interrupts the active {{[user]}} invocation and then runs {{[user]}}. The test previously asserted the old transient behavior: {{DISABLING}} state and zero {{[user]}} invocations immediately after calling {{disableControllerService()}}.

Because disable is asynchronous, the test can pass or fail depending on timing. The test should wait for the returned disable future and verify the final {{DISABLED}} state with one {{[user]}} invocation.

