## The task
Issue NIFI-16378 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Connector fails to drain if flow contains a disabled Processor
Area: Core Framework

If a Connector has a disabled processor, the drain never completes. This appears to be a bug in the Processor Lifecycle code:
{code:java}
public CompletableFuture<Void> stop() {
    return processScheduler.stopProcessor(processorNode, ProcessorStopLifecycleMethods.TRIGGER_ALL);
}{code}

This differs from the ProcessGroup Lifecycle code, which already skips any Processor that is stopped or disabled. We should similarly return a Completed future from this method if the Processor is already stopped or disabled

