## The task
Issue NIFI-14553 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: NPE in ListSmb due to DFS folders having no target mapping

When ListSmb is used for listing SMB Distributed File System (DFS) and there is a leaf folder in the DFS namespace that has no target mapping, it results in NullPointerException. Even though the unmapped folder is a configuration issue in the DFS namespace, the processor should not fail with an unhandled exception.

The NPE comes from the underlying smbj library. Related bug report: [https://github.com/[user]/smbj/issues/869]

Until it is fixed in the 3rd party library, a workaround should be applied on NiFi side.

## What this person changed
- NIFI-14553 Workaround for NPE in ListSmb due to DFS folders having no target mapping
  NIFI-14553 Workaround for NPE in ListSmb due to DFS folders having no target mapping

This closes #9925.
