## What they wrote in the discussion
- Notes on the solution:
 * the new "Connection Validation" property must be set to "false" if the SMB server does not support SMB2 ECHO requests outside of an active session
 * an alternative failover mechanism was added to avoid stale connections but it works only in non-DFS environments (when the NiFi client has direct access to the single SMB connection in use and can reconnect if it is needed)
 * health check of internal DFS connections could be implemented in the smbj library itself (see also [https://github.com/[user]/smbj/issues/796])

