## The task
Issue NIFI-14675 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Literal Long values can cause exceptions and lose precision in Record Path

1. precision loss

GreaterThanFilter, GreaterThanOrEqualFilter, LessThanFilter, LessThanOrEqualFilter convert incoming numbers to doubles, which introduces errors when comparing long numbers that exceed mantissa capacity for doubles.

Instead, if both numbers are long compatible: i.e. Long, Integer, Short and Byte, they should be compared as longs.

2. long literals

When using a long number in a RecordPath, a NumberFormatException occurs.

If the number is quoted, everything works as expected.

## What this person changed
- NIFI-14675 Improved support for Long literals in Record Path (#10030)
