## The task
Issue NIFI-15180 (Improvement, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Log initialization errors in ConsumeKinesis
Area: Extensions

`ConsumeKinesis` processor launches KCL scheduler under the hood. If scheduler initialization fails for any reason, it's visible in the application logs only. The processor continues running tasks, without any flow files produced.

Instead, the error should be propagated to the processor's code and then logged by a `ConsumeKinesis` processor's logger. 

It seems that `WorkerStateChangeListener` in the KCL's `coordinatorConfig` is the right candidate.

