## The task
Issue NIFI-14906 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Minor)
Title: ListenHTTP provides FlowFile package name to contained FlowFiles

Scenario: One or more FlowFiles are packaged into a single FFv3 FlowFile package using PackageFlowFile. Using InvokeHTTP, the FlowFile package is sent to ListenHTTP. InvokeHTTP is configured to send all attributes (or at least `filename` attribute) in the HTTP headers (Request Header Attributes Pattern property.)  ListenHTTP receives a FFv3 packaged FlowFile sent by InokeHTTP.

ListenHTTP automatically unpacks the FFv3 package into individual FlowFiles.  However, the filename of all FlowFiles is the filename of the FFv3 package FlowFile. The original filenames within the package are lost.

Proper behavior would allow the unpacked FlowFile to retain its original filename.

