## The task
Issue NIFI-14758 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: Decommission of primary node should wait for new primary node

When decommissioning a node, if the node being decommissioned is the cluster coordinator, there is a period of time where a new coordinator has not been elected yet, in Kubernetes this is the 15 second lease expiration, and if the decommission proceeds through the remaining steps when it removes it self from the cluster, it can result in the new coordinator still having a reference to the decommissioned node.

