## The task
Issue NIFI-14629 (Bug, Resolved, Fixed, priority Major)
Title: ConsumeKinesisStream backpressure handling may be blocked under load
Area: Extensions

In NIFI-14358 I added backpressure handling in ConsumeKinesisStream. The processor gets scheduled even when the output queue is full, in which case it stops producing records.

The processor may not be triggered on overwhelmed nodes in which case it will not get backpressured and will continue to overwhelm.

There should be a stop mechanism added that would trigger when the processor is not triggered for X amount of time. 3 seconds?

